+
+## 2026-10-05: the API reference, typedoc at deploy time
+
+Expected, from the rulings above: `deploy-site.yml` gains Node, pnpm, install, build and a typedoc
+run into `site/docs/api/`; DEPLOY.md's "no build" sentence is rewritten; typedoc becomes a root
+devDependency. Found and settled:
+
+- **typedoc 0.28.20**, exact, at the root (`pnpm add -D -w`; TypeScript 6.0.3 is in its peer
+  range, `5.0.x` through `6.0.x`). `pnpm site:api` runs it; every option is in the root
+  `typedoc.json`, so the script is the bare command and the output path lives in one place. The
+  lockfile is pnpm's: the same `pnpm add`, run from this commit's parent in a scratch copy of the
+  manifests, wrote it byte for byte. Besides typedoc's own tree it re-resolves one optional peer,
+  core's vitest and vite now naming esbuild 0.27.7 where they named 0.28.2; both versions were
+  already installed, and the frozen install accepts it.
+- **One root config with explicit `entryPoints` over a solution-style tsconfig, not the
+  `packages` strategy.** The twenty-two entry points are the twelve `src/index.ts` and every
+  subpath each package's `exports` names: `core/client`, `core/renderer`,
+  `renderer-solid/compiler`, `renderer-lit/hydration-support` (a leaf, not an index) and the
+  `client` of each of the six framework renderers. `tsconfig.typedoc.json` has `files: []` and a
+  `references` entry per package: typedoc's `getEntryPrograms` (read in `dist/node-utils.js`)
+  creates one program per referenced project when the root program has no files, each under
+  that package's own compiler options, and `getEntryPointsForPaths` finds each entry in whichever
+  program holds it. That matters because the packages' options differ (`lib` with and without
+  `DOM`, three JSX configurations, `useDefineForClassFields` off for Lit), and one flat program
+  would type-check every package under one of them. Only the programs holding an entry point are
+  diagnosed (`getPreEmitDiagnostics` over the entries' programs), so the empty root program's
+  references to projects that are not `composite` never fire. The `packages` strategy was the
+  alternative; typedoc's README says that mode "requires configuration to be present in each
+  directory", twelve more config files where one does the work.
+- **Typedoc reads the sources, not `dist/`.** The base tsconfig's `paths` map every published
+  specifier to its `src`, so a package's program reaches its neighbours' sources; run with every
+  `dist/` moved aside, typedoc wrote the same clean reference. The deploy builds first anyway, as
+  ruled, so a tree whose packages do not build publishes nothing.
+- **Each entry file names itself.** Typedoc names an entry by its path from the common root
+  (`core/src`, `core/src/client`), which nobody imports. Each of the twenty-two files carries
+  `/** @module @assemblejs/core/client */` and the like directly after its header: the rename is
+  typedoc's own (`onDeclaration` in `dist/index.js` sets a module's name from the tag, and a
+  comment carrying `@module` is taken as the file's comment, never a declaration's). A comment is
+  not a declaration, and the organization gate, run on the tree, is clean. The reference lists
+  the specifiers a user writes.
+- **Clean with `treatWarningsAsErrors`**: 22 modules, 416 pages, about 30 s locally, and no
+  `.nojekyll`. Watched red: an entry naming a file that does not exist stops it at exit 3 with
+  nothing written. Typedoc's `notExported` validation is on by default and fired on nothing, so no
+  type reached from a public signature is left unexported. `excludeExternals` keeps Fastify's and
+  the frameworks' types out; `excludeInternal` honours `@internal`; `githubPages: false` keeps a
+  `.nojekyll` out of a bucket that does not read it; `readme: "none"` starts the reference on the
+  module list, since the product README is the repository's; `cacheBust` adds the generation time
+  to the stylesheet and script links, because the deploy caches assets for seven days and the
+  search index and navigation are scripts that change with every run. The generated tree carries
+  none of the identity gate's strings.
+- **Source links are a claim CI alone proves.** Typedoc looks for a `.git` directory upward from
+  each source (`discoverPossibleGitDirs` in `dist/index.js`) and links a file only if that
+  repository's `git ls-files` lists it. From a worktree, whose `.git` is a file, it reaches the
+  main checkout, which does not list the worktree's paths, so the pages say "Defined in
+  packages/core/src/server/create-server.ts:65" without a link. The deploy's checkout is a clone
+  whose `origin` is GitHub, where the link template becomes GitHub's at the checked-out commit; a
+  checkout with no readable `origin` would warn, and the warning fails the run. The first
+  Actions run is where the links are seen.
+- **`pages.json` marks the page `generated`; `check-site.mjs` reads it.** A generated page is
+  exempt from the exists-locally check, still counts as declared for the link check, and the
+  directory it heads is not walked, because the generated tree links its own pages, which nobody
+  declares: with the tree on disk and the mark removed the real gate reports 1645 such links,
+  and with the tree absent it reports the missing page. The self-test, which covered only the
+  skin, now builds a scratch site and requires red on a declared page that is missing, clean on
+  the same page marked generated, and clean once the generated tree exists with undeclared links
+  inside it. Watched red four ways, each restored by the inverse edit and checked byte for byte:
+  the exemption removed, the skip removed, the missing-page refusal removed, and generated pages
+  dropped from the declared set. `site-links.mjs` needs no change: the page is not `in_nav`, has
+  no links region, and a page not on disk is skipped. The docs index gains a Reference section
+  linking `api/index.html`; the footers were regenerated and did not change.
+- **`deploy-site.yml`**: after the kit is staged, `pnpm/action-setup` and `actions/setup-node` at
+  the shas `ci.yml` pins, Node 22, the frozen install, `pnpm build`, `pnpm site:api`, and a step
+  that fails when `site/docs/api/index.html` is absent, all before "Check the site", which
+  exempts the page and so cannot prove it; that step, run locally from the YAML, passed with the
+  tree and failed without it. The sync steps are unchanged and already carry the reference: the
+  HTML sync includes every `.html`, and the asset sync excludes only `.md`, `.html` and `.json`,
+  which leaves typedoc's `.css`, `.js` and `.svg` in; it emits no fonts and no JSON. The top
+  comment and DEPLOY.md now say that two directories are written at deploy time, `kit/` and
+  `docs/api/`, where they said "no build". Validated with Python's yaml reader; the run itself
+  waits on `RELEASES_PAT`, as every deploy here does.
+- **The paths filter stays `site/**`, as ruled.** The reference refreshes on a push that touches
+  the site, not on one that touches only the packages; the next site push or a manual dispatch
+  catches it up. Said in DEPLOY.md and the workflow comment. If the owner wants a packages push
+  to republish, the include list gains `packages/*/src/**`, `typedoc.json` and
+  `tsconfig.typedoc.json`; not done here, because it changes what a push to `next` publishes.
+- **What else walks the tree.** The emoji and identity gates read `git ls-files`; jscpd honours
+  `.gitignore` and ignores `**/docs/**`; knip's project globs name `scripts/` and `browser/`. But
+  `eslint .` reads no ignore file of git's and, with a preview on disk, lints typedoc's bundled
+  `assets/*.js` to 347 errors (watched with the ignore removed), so `eslint.config.js` ignores
+  `site/docs/api/**` and says why. knip accepts typedoc because `site:api` runs its binary; with
+  the script removed it reports typedoc as an unused devDependency (watched). syncpack sees one
+  version.
