+`renderer-lit/hydration-support`, and the `client` of each of the six framework renderers) and
+writes the reference into `docs/api/`. It reads the sources, not `dist/`; the build runs first
+so that a tree whose packages do not build publishes nothing. The entry points are read through
+`tsconfig.typedoc.json`, a solution-style tsconfig whose `references` are the packages' own, so
+typedoc type-checks each package under its own options; each entry file names itself with a
+`@module` comment, so the reference reads by the specifier a user imports. Locally,
+`pnpm build && pnpm site:api` writes the same tree for preview.
